# filevault

Uploads for filevault.

The extension of a filename is the text after the LAST dot, lowercased: 'Archive.TAR.GZ' has extension 'gz', 'photo.JPG' has 'jpg'. A name with no dot, or a trailing dot, has no extension (empty string). The content type is looked up from the extension.

## Content type

contentType(name) maps the extension to a MIME type, defaulting to application/octet-stream.

## Safe names

safeName(name) strips any leading dots and slashes, then replaces characters outside [A-Za-z0-9._-] with an underscore, so a stored name can never climb a directory.
